---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="Privacy" description="Your files never leave your browser. What Animated SVG GO stores, and what it doesn't.">
  <div class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-lg">Your files never leave your browser.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="never-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="never-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">What we never do</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
        <li>Upload your files. Every step runs on your machine.</li>
        <li>Ask for an account, a name or an email.</li>
        <li>Show ads, or sell anything about you.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="analytics-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="analytics-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Counting visits</h2>
      <p>
        We count page views with Vercel Web Analytics, so we can see which pages people use and what to build next. For each view it records
        the page, the site that sent you, your country and city, and your browser, system and device type.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's anonymous. Visits are grouped by a hash of the request, which is thrown away after 24 hours. Vercel says it uses no third-party
        cookies and can't follow you across other sites. It never sees your files, because they never leave your browser. Read
        <a class="link" href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel's notes on analytics privacy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="search-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="search-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Searching for icons</h2>
      <p>
        The editor can search free icons from <a class="link" href="https://iconify.design">Iconify</a>. Nothing is sent until you press
        Search. Then your browser asks Iconify's servers for your search words and the matching icons. Like any website, Iconify sees your IP
        address and browser when it answers. Read <a class="link" href="https://iconify.design/privacy/">Iconify's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>Your own files are never sent. An icon you pick is loaded into the editor and stays in your browser, like any file you open.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="stored-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="stored-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">What stays in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        The last file you opened, and its effects, are saved in this browser's own storage so they're there when you come back. Only this
        browser on this machine can see them. Opening another file replaces them. To remove them, clear this site's data in your browser
        settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="hosting-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="hosting-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by <a class="link" href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel</a>. Like any web host, it keeps standard
        request logs when you load a page, such as your IP address and browser. Your files are never in them, because they are never sent.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Page>
